From: mscharged-port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] SPIR-V validation follows the backend debug layers
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host performance, no behaviour change.

Dawn runs spirv-val on the SPIR-V that Tint generates for every pipeline, even
when its blob cache already holds the compiled result, which adds to the
pipeline-creation stalls at scene transitions. It is a debug check of Dawn's
own compiler output: the generated SPIR-V, robustness and Dawn's command
validation are unchanged. Disable the enable_spirv_validation toggle when the
backend debug layers are off (the player setting graphics_validation=false);
validated runs and tests keep it. Apply after 0070.
diff --git a/lib/webgpu/gpu.cpp b/lib/webgpu/gpu.cpp
index 84446e2..15a346d 100644
--- a/lib/webgpu/gpu.cpp
+++ b/lib/webgpu/gpu.cpp
@@ -987,12 +987,15 @@ bool initialize(AuroraBackend auroraBackend, bool allowCpu) {
     };
     // Backend debug layers are independent of Dawn command validation and
     // robust buffer/shader access, which remain enabled in every build.
-    constexpr std::array disableToggles{
+    std::vector<const char*> disableToggles{
         "timestamp_quantization",
         // Adreno strikes again!
         // https://github.com/TwilitRealm/dusklight/issues/2563
         "use_spirv_reconvergence_mode",
     };
+    // spirv-val of Tint's output is a debug check, run on every pipeline even
+    // when the blob cache hits. It follows the backend debug layers.
+    if (!g_config.enableBackendValidation) disableToggles.push_back("enable_spirv_validation");
     wgpu::DawnTogglesDescriptor togglesDescriptor(wgpu::DawnTogglesDescriptor::Init{
         .nextInChain = &cacheDescriptor,
         .enabledToggleCount = enableToggles.size(),
